# {{ o.name }}

Firmware for **{{ t.display }}** with a [WireWeaver]({{ WW_GIT }}) device API served over
{{ "USB" if ww.usb else "RTT (debug probe)" }}.

| directory | |
|---|---|
| `{{ ww.api }}/` | `#![no_std]` API crate: the `{{ ww.trait }}` trait and its data types. Shared by the firmware and host-side clients |
| `firmware/` | the firmware (see `firmware/README.md`); `src/ww.rs` implements the API{{ ", `bootloader/` inside" if o.bootloader else "" }} |

The root `Cargo.toml` is a workspace of the API crate (with a `Cargo.lock`, which `#[ww_api_root]` needs to find the
API's git dependencies); the firmware is a standalone crate next to it, excluded from the workspace: it builds for
`{{ t.rust_target }}` with its own `.cargo/config.toml` and `Cargo.lock`.

## Build and run

```
cd firmware
cargo run
```

{% if t.family == "rp" %}
Without a probe free: hold BOOTSEL and reset, then `just flash-bootsel [SERIAL]` writes the ELF
straight through PICOBOOT (`ww dfu rp flash`), no picotool/elf2uf2/objcopy step.

{% endif %}
## Talk to the device

{% if ww.usb %}
Connect the MCU's USB (VID:PID `{{ "%04x:%04x" | format(*s.usb_id) }}`). `ww list` shows it with its API name, `ww introspect` prints the API
tree read from the device. `ww` is the WireWeaver CLI:
`cargo install --git {{ WW_GIT }} wire_weaver_cli` (on Linux USB access needs a udev rule, see its `docs/cli.md`).
{% else %}
The API runs on RTT channels `ww_up` / `ww_down`, next to the log output. Stop `cargo run` (probe-rs) first: a
probe can only be opened once, the firmware keeps running.
{% endif %}

A Rust host client is generated from `{{ ww.api }}` with
`wire_weaver::ww_codegen!({{ ww.krate }} :: {{ ww.trait }} for MyClient, client = "std_client")`
and the `wire_weaver_client` crate{{ " (feature `rtt`, `ClientConfig::rtt(<probe-rs chip>, None)`)" if ww.rtt else "" }}, see `examples/blinky` in
the WireWeaver repository.

## Changing the API

1. Add methods / properties / streams to `{{ ww.trait }}` in `{{ ww.api }}/src/lib.rs` (see `docs/api/overview.md`
   in the WireWeaver repository).
2. Implement them on `ServerState` in `firmware/src/ww.rs`; the compiler lists what is missing.
3. Bump the `{{ ww.api }}` version: the name + version identify the API to hosts.

`{{ ww.api }}/api_snapshots/` keeps a snapshot of its traits and types per version, and a test of the API crate
(`{{ ww.api }}/tests/evolution.rs`, `just api-check`, part of `just test`) requires the snapshot of the version in
`Cargo.toml`, comparing the source with it and that snapshot with the previous version's
([WireWeaver's evolution rules]({{ WW_GIT }}/blob/master/docs/evolution/rules.md)): it fails when the current
version has no snapshot yet, when the source differs from it, or when the API changed without the version bump the
change needs, and names the version to put into `{{ ww.api }}/Cargo.toml`. Save (or refresh) the current version's
snapshot with `just api-save` and commit the file; once a version is released, its snapshot never changes again.
`just hooks` (also run by `just setup`) turns on `.githooks/pre-commit`, which runs the check when a commit touches
the API crate; it chains after the hooks already in `.git/hooks/` and leaves `core.hooksPath` alone.
